[
  {
    "lesson_id": "013",
    "trigger_word": "orchestra",
    "trigger_card_number": 212,
    "title": "LESSON 13: EVERYDAY GREEK II",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "Twenty more that English took whole, most",
          "of them out of the theater and out of",
          "public life. Each kept the Greek noun and",
          "carried the sense somewhere new.",
          "",
          "  orchestra  ὀρχήστρα  dancing floor",
          "  scene      σκηνή     tent",
          "  crisis     κρίσις    a decision",
          "  character  χαρακτήρ  an engraved mark",
          "",
          "The orchestra was the round floor where",
          "the chorus danced; the skene was the hut",
          "behind it where actors changed. A crisis",
          "was the day a fever turned.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 20 CARDS: Greek taken whole."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 13"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "014",
    "trigger_word": "period",
    "trigger_card_number": 232,
    "title": "LESSON 14: PERI, DIA, EPI",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "Greek has its own prefixes, separate from",
          "Latin's and just as regular. PERI (περί)",
          "is around, DIA (διά) is across or",
          "through, EPI (ἐπί) is upon.",
          "",
          "  period      around + a way",
          "  periphery   around + carrying",
          "  diagnosis   through + knowledge",
          "  epitaph     upon + a tomb",
          "",
          "Read them in order and the sense builds.",
          "A pericardium is the sac around the",
          "heart; an epicenter is the point upon",
          "the center of an earthquake.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 16 CARDS: peri-, dia-, epi-."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 14"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "015",
    "trigger_word": "system",
    "trigger_card_number": 248,
    "title": "LESSON 15: SYN, ANA, CATA, APO",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "SYN (σύν) is together, ANA (ἀνά) is up or",
          "back, KATA (κατά) is down or thoroughly,",
          "APO (ἀπό) is away or off.",
          "",
          "  synthesis    together + a placing",
          "  analysis     back + a loosening",
          "  catastrophe  down + a turning",
          "  apostle      away + sent",
          "",
          "Synthesis and analysis are opposites, a",
          "placing together against a taking apart.",
          "",
          "Syn- changes shape before some letters:",
          "system, symmetry, syllable. It is the",
          "same prefix each time.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 21 CARDS: syn-, ana-, cata-, apo-."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 15"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "016",
    "trigger_word": "endoscope",
    "trigger_card_number": 269,
    "title": "LESSON 16: IN, OUT, AFTER, UNDER",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "ENDO (ἔνδον) is within, EXO (ἔξω) and",
          "ECTO (ἐκτός) are outside, META (μετά) is",
          "after or beyond, HYPO (ὑπό) is under.",
          "",
          "  endoscope      within + viewer",
          "  exoskeleton    outside + skeleton",
          "  metamorphosis  after + form",
          "  hypodermic     under + skin",
          "",
          "Endo- and exo- divide the body between",
          "them: endocrine glands pour inward,",
          "exocrine glands out onto the skin.",
          "",
          "Hypo- is the low half of the hyper- pair.",
          "Hypothermia is too little heat.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 19 CARDS: in, out, after, under."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 16"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "017",
    "trigger_word": "logic",
    "trigger_card_number": 288,
    "title": "LESSON 17: WORD AND LAW",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "LOGOS (λόγος) is word, speech, reason.",
          "NOMOS (νόμος) is law or custom, and as an",
          "ending -nomy is the ordering of a whole",
          "field.",
          "",
          "  prologue     before + words",
          "  epilogue     after + words",
          "  economy      household + law",
          "  astronomy    star + law",
          "",
          "Autonomy is making your own law.",
          "Taxonomy is the law of arrangement,",
          "which is to say classification.",
          "",
          "Gastronomy is the law of the stomach,",
          "and means the art of eating well.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 10 CARDS: log and -nomy."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 17"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "018",
    "trigger_word": "epidemic",
    "trigger_card_number": 298,
    "title": "LESSON 18: PEOPLE AND CITY",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "DEMOS (δῆμος) is the people. POLIS",
          "(πόλις) is the city, meaning the whole",
          "city-state and its citizens.",
          "",
          "  epidemic     upon + the people",
          "  pandemic     all + the people",
          "  demagogue    the people + leading",
          "  metropolis   mother + city",
          "",
          "Politics is the affairs of the polis.",
          "Police and policy come from the same word",
          "through Latin politia, the running of a",
          "city.",
          "",
          "An epidemic falls upon one people; a",
          "pandemic falls upon all of them.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 13 CARDS: dem and polit."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 18"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "019",
    "trigger_word": "monarch",
    "trigger_card_number": 311,
    "title": "LESSON 19: RULE AND TIME",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "ARCHE (ἀρχή) means both first and rule,",
          "and the two senses split in English.",
          "CHRONOS (χρόνος) is time.",
          "",
          "  monarch      one + ruler",
          "  architect    chief + builder",
          "  archaic      of the beginning",
          "  chronometer  time + measure",
          "",
          "Where arch- means chief you get the",
          "archbishop and the archenemy; where it",
          "means first or old you get the archaic",
          "and the archetype.",
          "",
          "Chronic means drawn out over time, not",
          "severe. Its opposite is acute.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 15 CARDS: arch and chron."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 19"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "020",
    "trigger_word": "pyrotechnic",
    "trigger_card_number": 326,
    "title": "LESSON 20: CRAFT AND ORDER",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "TECHNE (τέχνη) is art or craft. MECHANE",
          "(μηχανή) is a device. KOSMOS (κόσμος) is",
          "order, and so the ordered universe.",
          "",
          "  technique     craft + method",
          "  polytechnic   many + crafts",
          "  mechanic      device + worker",
          "  cosmology     order + study",
          "",
          "Kosmos had a second sense, ornament, and",
          "English kept both: the cosmos is the",
          "ordered whole, cosmetics are what put a",
          "face in order.",
          "",
          "A cosmopolitan is a citizen of the world,",
          "kosmos joined to polis.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 16 CARDS: techn, mech, cosm."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 20"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "021",
    "trigger_word": "criticism",
    "trigger_card_number": 342,
    "title": "LESSON 21: -ISM, -IST, -IZE",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "Three Greek endings do much of the work",
          "in English: -ISM (-ισμός) a doctrine or a",
          "practice, -IST (-ιστής) the one who",
          "practices it, -IZE (-ίζειν) to make.",
          "",
          "  criticism    the practice of judging",
          "  pharmacist   one who deals in drugs",
          "  organize     to make into a system",
          "",
          "They take any stem at all: capitalism,",
          "dentist, tourist and modernize are all",
          "Latin words wearing Greek endings.",
          "",
          "Two keep their old pictures. Enthusiasm",
          "is the god within; sarcasm is the",
          "tearing of flesh.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 19 CARDS: -ism, -ist and -ize."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 21"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "022",
    "trigger_word": "aristocracy",
    "trigger_card_number": 361,
    "title": "LESSON 22: RULE AND RULERS",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "KRATOS (κράτος) is power: -CRACY",
          "(-κρατία) is rule by, -CRAT (-κράτης) the",
          "one who rules. ARCHE (ἀρχή) is rule as",
          "well, and -ARCHY names the system.",
          "",
          "  aristocracy   the best + rule",
          "  plutocracy    wealth + rule",
          "  oligarchy     few + rule",
          "  anarchy       without + rule",
          "",
          "The first part names who holds it: demos",
          "the people, theos a god, autos himself,",
          "hieros the priests.",
          "",
          "Bureaucracy is rule by the desk, a French",
          "office on a Greek ending.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 18 CARDS: -cracy and -archy."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 22"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "023",
    "trigger_word": "pathetic",
    "trigger_card_number": 379,
    "title": "LESSON 23: FEELING, LOVE, WISDOM",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "PATHOS (πάθος) is anything that befalls",
          "you: feeling, suffering, disease. PHILIA",
          "(φιλία) is love, SOPHIA (σοφία) wisdom.",
          "",
          "  sympathy      together + feeling",
          "  empathy       into + feeling",
          "  apathy        without + feeling",
          "  philanthropy  love + humankind",
          "",
          "Pathology is the study of disease, but",
          "pathetic is about pity: the same root at",
          "its two ends.",
          "",
          "The sophists were paid teachers of",
          "argument, so sophistry now means clever",
          "reasoning that is not sound.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 16 CARDS: path, phil and soph."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 23"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "024",
    "trigger_word": "atheist",
    "trigger_card_number": 395,
    "title": "LESSON 24: NOT, BAD, WELL, BOTH",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "A (ἀ-) is not or without, DYS (δυς-) is",
          "bad or difficult, EU (εὖ) is well, AMPHI",
          "(ἀμφί) is both or around.",
          "",
          "  atheist      without + god",
          "  dyslexia     difficult + words",
          "  euphoria     well + bearing",
          "  amphibian    both + life",
          "",
          "The a- takes an n before a vowel: apathy",
          "but anemia, atypical but anonymous. It",
          "is one prefix, not two.",
          "",
          "Eu- and dys- are a pair. A euphemism",
          "speaks well of a thing; dystopia is",
          "utopia turned bad.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 22 CARDS: not, bad, well, both."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 24"
      }
    ]
  }
]
